{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"illdefined-pearl-cony","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# The close gate offers `--force-close` as the remedy for a RESOURCE exhaustion\n\nDiscovered while root-causing [rebar:bf31-fd55-d28d-4b7a].\n\nWhen completion verification fails for ANY reason, `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:293-297`\nappends `Override with --force-close=\"<reason>\".` to the error. That is correct for a verdict the\noperator wants to overrule. It is wrong for a **resource** failure, where no verdict exists at all.\n\nA step-budget exhaustion is not a judgment that the work is incomplete — it is the gate failing to\nfinish evaluating. Conflating the two points the operator at the one action the project forbids: a\nforce-closed ticket is the unattested state epic [rebar:e369-a449-4773-48fb] spent its whole cycle\nremoving, and the reason [rebar:b586-2fda-8a15-4260] and [rebar:0059-c7f0-cce1-4077] were reopened.\nSame shape as the certification trap in [rebar:738a-376e-4829-42ca]: two individually correct rules\ncomposing into a state whose only reachable exit is the forbidden one.\n\nThe remedy text itself was already narrowed once for this class — `close_gate_remedy`\n(`src/rebar/llm/failure.py:522-550`) stops blaming a missing `[agents]` extra for a verifier that\nprovably ran (bug d59e). This is the same correction one step further out: the `--force-close`\nsentence is appended unconditionally, after the remedy.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a completion verification that fails from RESOURCE exhaustion (step budget / iteration cap)\n      does not present `--force-close` as its remedy\n- [ ] the message instead names the actionable next move for a resource failure and points at the\n      recorded diagnostic\n- [ ] a genuine FAIL verdict still offers `--force-close` exactly as today (regression pinned)\n- [ ] a test asserts the two failure classes produce different remedy text","id":"218e-0ec1-385d-493a","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Close gate offers --force-close as the remedy for a RESOURCE exhaustion, steering agents into the unattested state"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785932647945583001,"uuid":"69d4598c-0d5a-4734-9c6e-5bb6e1f0ff49"}